            ["How does the cloud security assessment process work?", "We begin by understanding your cloud infrastructure and defining the assessment scope. We then review security settings and access controls before evaluating identified risks and delivering a report with prioritized findings and remediation recommendations."],
            ["How often should a cloud security assessment be conducted?", "Businesses should consider conducting a cloud security assessment annually and after major infrastructure changes, cloud migrations or significant application updates. Environments that handle sensitive data may require more frequent assessments based on their risk exposure."],
            ["What are the common cloud security risks?", "Common cloud security risks include excessive user permissions, exposed storage, weak network controls, insecure configurations, inadequate monitoring and poorly managed credentials. These weaknesses can increase the risk of unauthorized access and data breaches."],
            ["Can cloud security assessments help with compliance?", "Yes. Cloud security assessments can identify gaps in security controls against relevant standards and regulatory requirements. Depending on the scope, reviews may reference CIS Benchmarks and other applicable frameworks to support compliance preparation and audit activities."],
            ["What do we receive after a cloud security assessment?", "You receive a report summarizing identified security risks and their potential impact. Depending on the agreed scope, the deliverables may include detailed findings, supporting evidence, compliance gaps and practical recommendations for improving cloud security."],
            ["What is the difference between cloud security assessment and cloud penetration testing?", "A cloud security assessment reviews configurations, access controls and security practices to identify weaknesses. Cloud penetration testing involves authorized attempts to exploit selected vulnerabilities to understand their potential impact. Both approaches can complement each other as part of a broader cloud security strategy."],
            ["How do we choose the right cloud security company?", "Look for a cloud security company that understands your cloud platform and business requirements and provides clear findings with actionable recommendations. Experience with AWS, Azure and GCP security controls alongside recognized security benchmarks can help you evaluate a provider. Contact Cipher Trivia for more information."]
          ] %}
